```rust
Value::VLam(_) => {
    let probe = Rc::new(Value::VNeutral(depth, Vec::new()));
    let body_val = apply(value, probe);
    lam(quote(depth + 1, &body_val))
}
```

The `_` pattern is Rust idiom for "deliberately ignored" — it documents intent rather than triggering warnings. (Why not apply the `closure` directly? Because `apply` takes a `&ValueRef` and *is* the single dispatcher for "call any value" — keeping one dispatcher is better design than reaching inside closures from two places.)

